<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Maceo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Antonio Maceo Grajales</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Maceo was a Cuban general of the wars of independence, nicknamed the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> Titan'. An Afro-Cuban from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, he rose through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> and rejected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-zanjon">Pact of Zanjón</a> in the Protest of Baraguá in 1878. Returning in 1895, he led the invasion of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximo-gomez">Máximo Gómez</a> and was killed in battle at San Pedro in December 1896.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-maceo.jpg" alt="Antonio Maceo" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antonio_Maceo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
